=== meta ===
bypass: 125
rule: TEST_DISABLED
title: a helper imported package-relative, whose own helper raises the skip, disables the test that starts calling it
origin: #272, ruling 272.Q2 (a) — `from .support import requires_db` resolves beside the test, as an imported
origin2: assertion helper does; the outcome lies one call further, in the helper module's own `_unavailable`
=== head: app/__init__.py ===
=== head: app/billing.py ===
def total(items):
    return round(sum(items), 2)
=== head: tests/__init__.py ===
=== head: tests/support.py ===
import unittest


def _unavailable(reason):
    raise unittest.SkipTest(reason)


def requires_db():
    _unavailable("no database")
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total([30, 48.75]) == 78.75
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import total

from .support import requires_db


def test_total():
    requires_db()
    assert total([30, 48.75]) == 78.75
=== expect ===
